## 1. Decision summary

| Need | Pick | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Script/outline/metadata generation | Claude (you already pay for this) | Free within your Pro usage window |
| Slides (native .pptx) | `python-pptx` (or Claude.ai's built-in PPT generation, exported) | Free, scriptable, editable output |
| PPTX → images | LibreOffice `--headless --convert-to png` | Free, reliable, cross-platform |
| Images + audio → video | FFmpeg + MoviePy | Industry-standard, free, scriptable |
| Voice cloning / narration | **Chatterbox** (Resemble AI, MIT license) as default; XTTS v2 as fallback for extra language coverage | MIT license = truly free for commercial use, GPU-accelerated, near-ElevenLabs quality with your own cloned voice |
| Transcription + word timestamps | **faster-whisper** for speed, **WhisperX** when you need tight word-level timing/chapters | Both free, local, MIT-ish licenses, no per-minute fee |
| Chapters/timestamp generation | Your own LLM-pass over the WhisperX word/segment output | Cheap, accurate, fully controllable |
| Long → Shorts | **Vantage** (your existing tool) reused as a module/service | Already built, open source, keyword-aware clipping |
| Subtitle burn-in | FFmpeg `drawtext`/`subtitles` filter, or `ffmpeg -vf subtitles=file.srt` | Free, no watermark |
| Publishing | YouTube Data API v3 (official, free quota) | Automates upload, thumbnail, description, tags, scheduling |

**Monthly cash cost once built:** effectively $0–5/month (electricity / occasional cloud GPU burst) instead of $29+/month for Slidespeak, assuming you have or rent a GPU (RTX 3060 12GB or better is comfortable for Chatterbox + WhisperX + faster-whisper together).

