## 4. Module notes (what to actually build first)

1. **`scriptwriter`** — one Claude call that returns strict JSON: slide titles, bullet text, per-slide speaker notes (the narration script), plus a second call for SEO title/description/tags/chapters skeleton. This is the highest-leverage module since it removes almost all manual writing.
2. **`slidebuilder`** — `python-pptx` reading that JSON into a branded template (your own `.pptx` master with fonts/colors set once). Keep it simple at first: title + bullets + optional image placeholder.
3. **`voice`** — wrap Chatterbox behind a small interface (`synthesize(text, voice_id) -> mp3_path`) so ElevenLabs can be swapped in for one high-stakes video without touching the rest of the pipeline.
4. **`video_assembler`** — LibreOffice batch-converts the deck to PNGs, then FFmpeg/MoviePy stretches each slide to match its audio clip's duration and concatenates. This is the part existing OSS repos (`ppt2video`, `ppt_presenter`, `py-ppt2movie`) already solve — start by forking one of those instead of writing from scratch.
5. **`transcriber`** — run WhisperX (`large-v3` or `distil-large-v3` if GPU-limited) on `final.mp4`'s audio track for word-level timestamps; this transcript feeds both chapters and subtitle burn-in.
6. **`chapters`** — a short Claude prompt that takes the WhisperX segment list and returns YouTube-style chapter markers (`00:00 Intro`, `01:32 Topic A`...), respecting YouTube's "first chapter must start at 0:00" rule.
7. **`shorts`** — don't rebuild this. Have `final.mp4` + `transcript.json` + your target keywords call into Vantage's existing logic (as a library import if it's structured that way, or as an HTTP call to a self-hosted instance).
8. **`publisher`** — YouTube Data API v3 upload with title/description/tags/chapters/thumbnail set programmatically; start with manual review before auto-publish (draft/private upload).

Build in this order: 1 → 2 → 4 → 3 → 5 → 6 → 8, then bolt on shorts (7) once the long-form path is solid, since it depends on transcript + final video already existing.

