### 2. Voice like ElevenLabs Professional Voice Cloning — not edge-tts

**edge-tts / macOS say = generic bot voices.** They are not your clone. That path is blocked by default (`voice.require_clone: true`).

#### How ElevenLabs PVC works (cloud)

| PVC | Guidance |
|-----|----------|
| Minimum | ~30 min clean speech |
| Sweet spot | 1–3 hours |
| Needs | Quiet room, single speaker, no music, consistent mic |
| Plan | Creator+ on ElevenLabs |
| Result | Server-side fine-tuned voice model |

You cannot export a PVC model into this repo. You can still **call** an ElevenLabs PVC `voice_id` later if you pay for it.

#### Local pro path in this project (MIT Chatterbox)

[Chatterbox](https://github.com/resemble-ai/chatterbox) (Resemble AI) is zero-shot cloning: it uses a **reference recording of you** and synthesizes new speech in that voice. Public blind tests have scored it competitively against ElevenLabs; it is free for commercial use under MIT.

It is **not** the same training process as PVC (no multi-hour fine-tune), but with a strong reference pack it is the right free/local target for “sounds like me, not a bot.”

